Let the function:
f(x) = \begin{cases} ax(x-1) + b & ; \quad x < 1 \\ x - 1 & ; \quad 1 \le x \le 3 \\ px^2 + qx + 2 & ; \quad x > 3 \end{cases}
If $f(x)$ is continuous for all $x$, $f'(1)$ does not exist, and $f'(x)$ is continuous at $x = 3$. Match the values in Column-I with Column-II: <table class="qx-match-list qx-match-table" border="1" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0"><tr><td>Column-I</td><td>Column-II</td></tr><tr><td>(A) a cannot have value</td><td>(P) 1/3</td></tr><tr><td>(B) b has value</td><td>(Q) 0</td></tr><tr><td>(C) p has value</td><td>(R) -1</td></tr><tr><td>(D) q has value</td><td>(S) 1</td></tr></table>
